# CASM WP20 trusted reference: casmexprn
#
# Independently hand-derived from the casmexprn fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Exercises the
# `<` (low-byte) and `>` (high-byte) operand operators in every operand
# position -- immediate, bare (address), indirect-indexed, .BYTE list,
# .WORD list -- and the addressing-mode selection that follows from the
# operator's result width.
#
# Source (.ORG $C000):
#   .ORG $C000            -> 00 C0   PRG load-address header (little-endian)
#   LDA #<$1234           -> A9 34   immediate; <$1234 = low byte = $34
#   LDA >$1234            -> A5 12   >$1234 = high byte = $12; no '#', value
#                                    < 256 -> zero-page addressing -> LDA $12
#   LDA (<$1234),Y        -> B1 34   (<$1234),Y = ($34),Y -> (indirect),Y
#   .BYTE <$1234, >$1234  -> 34 12   one byte each: $34, $12
#   .WORD <$1234, >$1234  -> 34 00 12 00   .WORD $0034, $0012 little-endian
#
# bytes: 14
# sha256: 325b48c21115fa9ac006a6aabfeecee08171a5d93b6746e701007bbb97e612b9
# source_sha256: casmexprn.seq=3ae1d05bd1022cc4bd266dbeaedd4838fbe33ef50fb6943dcbb81d4971ed6bd5

00 C0
A9 34 A5 12 B1 34
34 12 34 00 12 00
